# OpenSpec Core (Always On)

## Session protocol

1. Run `bash scripts/cursor-session-init.sh` at session start when doing non-trivial work.
2. Check `@DECISIONS.md` (last 5 ADRs) before architectural changes.
3. Route via `@AGENT.md`; load `@modules/*` only when the decision table points there.

## Non-negotiable

1. `@SAFETY.md` constraints apply to every task.
2. Verify before complete — follow `@IMPLEMENTATION.md` verification levels.
3. Serialized mutations: no parallel file writes / git mutations / destructive shell.
4. When in doubt, do less; ask instead of guessing.
5. Minimal diff; no TODOs in merged code.

## Cursor context discipline

- Use `@path` references instead of dumping whole files.
- Load `@IMPLEMENTATION.md` only when writing or reviewing code.
- Load `@MEMORY.md` only for long sessions, resume, or checkpoint work.
